From 85427c76108a1edc13a4ccdd578b51245d56efcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DjagbleyEmmanuel <djagbleyemmanuel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:49:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(lrc): port native synchronized lyric alignment

Ports the get_lrc pipeline from the HOT-Step fork of acestep.cpp: an
extra DiT pass for cross-attention alignment, DTW lyric-audio
alignment with bidirectional consensus, and LRC formatting.

Upstream lacks the LoRA/section parameters the fork's graph helpers
carry, so the alignment graph's self-attention call takes the upstream
argument list -- it passed nullptr for the LoRA parameter anyway.

The fork's X-LRC-Text header is emitted from ace-server rather than
hot-step-server; base64 is implemented locally for the one call site.
